  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are a mixed outcome: S1 is strict, S4 and S5 are acceptable, but S2 and S3 are weakened. S2 allows sales above the 5% test-failure cap until an 8% sales-stop threshold while giving customers numerical rates but not public disclosure. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 3 years and retrofit to at least 6 years, and S5 keeps a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with prompt (not fixed-day) customer notices."
